Comment (internal/api/handler/lineage_leverage.go:101):
**Medium (performance):** this builds the entire lineage engine to use only two of its fields.

`buildEngine(nil, nil)` runs `loadCatalogs` + `loadEdges` + `loadCompliance` (which calls `LoadLatestEvidenceStreams` — the whole latest-evidence corpus, the ~1s+ / hundreds-of-thousands-of-rows query the `evidence.go` comments warn about) + `loadRisks` + `loadLeverage` + `loadGlobalSSPScope` (every SSP's profile membership and implementation statuses). But `LeverageDetail` only reads `engine.controlCatalogType[ref]` (the existence 404 at line 106) and `engine.sspTitles[sspID]` (downstream titles at line 159). None of the evidence/risk/edge/impl-status loading is used.

The self-review note weighed only the *unused `Summarize`* overhead, not the whole-engine cost — and this is a per-control drawer endpoint, so it pays the full-corpus load every time a user opens the panel.

Suggest replacing the engine build with a targeted control-existence query + an SSP-title lookup keyed on the SSP ids `ProjectForControl` already returns.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Agreed — this is a real per-drawer cost and I under-weighed it in self-review (I only noted the unused Summarize, not the full evidence-corpus load). Fixing: LeverageDetail will drop buildEngine(nil,nil) entirely and instead (1) do a targeted control-existence 404 via a relational.Control lookup on (catalog_id, control_id), and (2) resolve downstream + upstream SSP titles in one Preload("Metadata") query keyed on the SSP ids ProjectForControl already returns. No evidence/risk/edge/impl-status loading.

